"answer_core": "I would not choose the hybrid direction yet. Treat two questions as gates, not vibes: does Dr. Silva actually have usable data you can access on a clear timeline, and is your fallback still advisor-backed, resourced, technically ready, identity-coherent, and protected by a stop-loss plan?\n\nKeep the political sequence clean. Talk to your advisor first. Use Dr. Silva only as a low-cost reality check on concrete data access, collaboration depth, and timing. Go to the committee only after you know whether the data path is real and whether your advisor would support the move without quietly pulling you back toward the safer lab path.\n\nFor the next two weeks, do dated evidence checks instead of building a finished proposal. Ask what data exists, who controls it, when you could inspect it, what authorship or collaboration terms would look like, and what work would still be yours. In parallel, test whether the fallback path can genuinely carry a dissertation if the Silva path fails.\n\nDo not run all three options in parallel. Do not treat broad PhD success-rate claims as calibrated probabilities for this case; use them only as humility checks. Choose the path only after the Silva/data gate and the fallback gate both have concrete evidence. The best path is not the hottest story; it is the one with a real chance of becoming a finishable PhD.",
